From 8d42b49d164b28f22c805e82c091b53843f1d565 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:21:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: material properties and external variables
 by variable

The material properties and the external state variables of a batch can
be given either as a group (one field) or variable by variable (one
field per variable), through the optional members
material_properties_by_variable and external_state_variables_by_variable
of the states. The second form allows a different layout per variable,
for instance uniform values for some material properties only, as in
MGIS. The structures initialized as before keep their meaning.

Both forms are converted on the host into the same description
(VariableFields, InputFields), passed by value to the kernels: the code
executed at each point does not depend on the form. The material
properties and the external state variables of a point are always
copied, so that the direct mode only depends on the other fields.

- PointTraits: number of components of each material property and of
  each external state variable (behaviours and models).
- SYCL backend: per variable fields copied on the device when needed.
- compare.cxx: third storage, by variable, with uniform values.
- documentation of the two forms.
